---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Contact | spousalsupportcalc.com';
const description = 'Contact spousalsupportcalc.com with corrections to formulas, state law updates, or feedback on guides.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Contact</h1>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We read every message.</p>

  <h2>What we respond to</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Corrections to formula citations or state statutes — if a formula percentage has changed, a state has amended its alimony law, or a case citation is outdated, let us know.</li>
    <li>Errors or unclear language in guides — if a guide is confusing, contains an inaccuracy, or omits something important, we want to know.</li>
    <li>Suggestions for new content — if there&rsquo;s a state, scenario, or topic we haven&rsquo;t covered that would be useful, we welcome requests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don&rsquo;t respond to</h2>
  <p>We can&rsquo;t evaluate your specific divorce situation, estimate what a judge would award in your case, or recommend specific attorneys. Spousal support outcomes depend on jurisdiction, individual facts, and judicial discretion that no formula or general guide can fully capture. For your situation, contact a family-law attorney in your state &mdash; most offer free or low-cost initial consultations. We also don&rsquo;t respond to partnership requests or solicitations for paid content placements.</p>
</BaseLayout>
